* wizlog4 - SUPERSEDED by wiz4up (the packet-mode server setup it relied on, wizsv4,
* is gone). Kept for by-hand use only: waits for the first client, then starts one
* listener on /wz0. Needs: a CIPMUX=1 packet server already running on port 23.
echo * WizFi360 Helper - Remote packet connection
echo * From the remote client connect to port 23 of
echo * the WizFi's IP address now...
echo AT+CIPSTA_CUR?>/wz
modem /wz
echo ATE0>/wz
modem /wz
modem -t0 /wz
iniz /wz0
xmode /wz0 eko=1
tsmon /wz0&
